# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file for the "Cite this repository"
# button, and Zenodo reads it when it archives a GitHub release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this app in research, a course or a benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "vulnerable-python: a deliberately vulnerable Python web app"
abstract: >-
  A deliberately vulnerable Flask application for security testing and
  training. Each endpoint passes one kind of untrusted input to one risky
  operation: a SQL query, a shell command, code evaluation, deserialization,
  a file path, an outbound request and more. Run it only on an isolated lab
  machine you control, and never deploy it.
authors:
